<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Sticky traps for rodents, introduced in India during the 1980-90s, have become a common household device to trap mice and lizards. However, sticky glue traps also capture non-target animals such as snakes, commonly causing them to die of suffocation, stress, dehydration, and starvation. This research presents data from Pune city, showing the death of six out of the seven snakes found stuck to sticky traps during rescue operations spread across 11 months. Researchers highlight the need for understanding the full impact of sticky traps on snakes.)
/Pg 7 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
