/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The Oriental garden lizard \(Calotes versicolor\) is an agamid lizard species and has a widespread distribution across south and southeast Asian countries. This species is known to feed on a variety of invertebrates, vertebrates, and even certain plants. Patel and Vyas \(2024\) report a novel finding of several oriental garden lizards feeding on shrimps at an aquaculture farm in Vadodara in April 2024. This was an uncommon sighting as they were previously observed feeding on insects and rarely any other prey.)
/E (The Oriental garden lizard \(Calotes versicolor\) is an agamid lizard species and has a widespread distribution across south and southeast Asian countries. This species is known to feed on a variety of invertebrates, vertebrates, and even certain plants. Patel and Vyas \(2024\) report a novel finding of several oriental garden lizards feeding on shrimps at an aquaculture farm in Vadodara in April 2024. This was an uncommon sighting as they were previously observed feeding on insects and rarely any other prey.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [13]
