/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (In a recent study, Khandekar et al. \(2024\) describe two new species of geckos, Cnemaspis basalticola and C. kalsubaiensis, through detailed genetic and morphological analyses. These species are part of the C. girii group and are distributed in the Northern Western Ghats in Maharashtra, India. C. basalticola is named after its habitat of basaltic rock cliffs, with its type locality at Ratangad Fort, Ahmednagar district. In contrast, C. kalsubaiensis is named after Kalsubai, the highest peak in Maharashtra and its type locality.)
/E (In a recent study, Khandekar et al. \(2024\) describe two new species of geckos, Cnemaspis basalticola and C. kalsubaiensis, through detailed genetic and morphological analyses. These species are part of the C. girii group and are distributed in the Northern Western Ghats in Maharashtra, India. C. basalticola is named after its habitat of basaltic rock cliffs, with its type locality at Ratangad Fort, Ahmednagar district. In contrast, C. kalsubaiensis is named after Kalsubai, the highest peak in Maharashtra and its type locality.)
