316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (The mugger crocodile \(Crocodylus palustris\) is a freshwater crocodilian species listed as Schedule I under the Wildlife Protection Act of India \(1972\). This species experiences a high degree of conflict with humans living adjacent to water bodies and faces other threats such as habitat fragmentation and pollution of rivers due to industrial waste. Vadodara, Gujarat, has a large population of muggers and is a hotspot for human-mugger conflict. Desai et al. \(2024\) assessed the physiological responses to stress using faecal glucocorticoid metabolite \(fGCM\) levels in free-ranging muggers in Gujarat. Their study revealed that muggers inhabiting urban and rural habitats, with high human-crocodile conflict and polluted water bodies, have significantly higher levels of fGCM compared to rural areas where people coexist with muggers. Elevated levels of glucocorticoids cause negative impacts on the physiology of species and indicate chronic stress.)
/E (The mugger crocodile \(Crocodylus palustris\) is a freshwater crocodilian species listed as Schedule I under the Wildlife Protection Act of India \(1972\). This species experiences a high degree of conflict with humans living adjacent to water bodies and faces other threats such as habitat fragmentation and pollution of rivers due to industrial waste. Vadodara, Gujarat, has a large population of muggers and is a hotspot for human-mugger conflict. Desai et al. \(2024\) assessed the physiological responses to stress using faecal glucocorticoid metabolite \(fGCM\) levels in free-ranging muggers in Gujarat. Their study revealed that muggers inhabiting urban and rural habitats, with high human-crocodile conflict and polluted water bodies, have significantly higher levels of fGCM compared to rural areas where people coexist with muggers. Elevated levels of glucocorticoids cause negative impacts on the physiology of species and indicate chronic stress.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [13]
>>
