/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Salazar's pit viper \(Trimeresurus salazar\) has been recently described from Northeast India. Individuals of this species have been observed from Assam and Meghalaya since then, and are identifiable due to their distinct morphology. In October 2021, the authors came across a pit viper individual in a garden in Agartala, Tripura. The female was later identified as Salazar's pit viper due to its distinguishable morphology and colouration. Thus, Choudhury et al. \(2024\) present the first record of this species from this region surmising its range extension. )
/E (Salazar's pit viper \(Trimeresurus salazar\) has been recently described from Northeast India. Individuals of this species have been observed from Assam and Meghalaya since then, and are identifiable due to their distinct morphology. In October 2021, the authors came across a pit viper individual in a garden in Agartala, Tripura. The female was later identified as Salazar's pit viper due to its distinguishable morphology and colouration. Thus, Choudhury et al. \(2024\) present the first record of this species from this region surmising its range extension. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
