422 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (Back in 2022, shortly after completing my undergraduate studies, I was engaged with a Zoological Society of London's EDGE fellow as a research intern focusing on the Dattatreya night frog \(Nyctibatrachus dattatreyaensis\) in Chikkamagaluru, Karnataka, India. )
/E (Back in 2022, shortly after completing my undergraduate studies, I was engaged with a Zoological Society of London's EDGE fellow as a research intern focusing on the Dattatreya night frog \(Nyctibatrachus dattatreyaensis\) in Chikkamagaluru, Karnataka, India. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
423 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (Every evening by 3:00 pm, I would gather my food, and equipment and load them into the car with my research advisor, the amazing Arpithamol, and my fellow intern and dear friend, Tania. We would then set off on our journey, listening to music and snacking along the way. The weather was often quiet, cold and misty, and my research advisor would make daring manoeuvres on the winding roads to Baba Budan Hills. Those moments are etched in my heart; the camaraderie and the determination to uncover the secrets of the Dattatreya night frog.)
/E (Every evening by 3:00 pm, I would gather my food, and equipment and load them into the car with my research advisor, the amazing Arpithamol, and my fellow intern and dear friend, Tania. We would then set off on our journey, listening to music and snacking along the way. The weather was often quiet, cold and misty, and my research advisor would make daring manoeuvres on the winding roads to Baba Budan Hills. Those moments are etched in my heart; the camaraderie and the determination to uncover the secrets of the Dattatreya night frog.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
424 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/T (As we prepared to venture, scouting for suitable locations to set up transects, I would begin by offering a whispered prayer to God, seeking protection from the bloodsucking leeches, but in vain. There were two crucial lessons I learned during this journey: to tread cautiously and never grasp onto an object without knowing its nature. Walking along the rocky path, with our leech socks and ponchos, amidst the squelchy mud, was almost like a bizarre spa day. )
/E (As we prepared to venture, scouting for suitable locations to set up transects, I would begin by offering a whispered prayer to God, seeking protection from the bloodsucking leeches, but in vain. There were two crucial lessons I learned during this journey: to tread cautiously and never grasp onto an object without knowing its nature. Walking along the rocky path, with our leech socks and ponchos, amidst the squelchy mud, was almost like a bizarre spa day. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
